AB  - Annotation. To test the dependence between the progression of the sport results (ended with the Polish records in the junior category in 10 and 20 km) and the training loading complied in the beginning years of the training of two Polish Olympic contestants in the sport walking (G.S.' s VII th place in 50 km and B.K.' s XII th place in 20 km). Is any directly proportional dependence between the result pace of the sport walking in 10 and 20 km ended with the polish records in the junior category in both distances and the training structure and quantity and intensity of the training loading. The appearance of the tendency to the stabilisation of the sport results development's pace can be a succession of too significant training loading in the junior category. There is a possibility of holding the relative stabilisation of the sport development in the sport walking for a long time. The training quantity and its intensity on the oxygen-non-oxygen level can influence on the result progression in 10 and 20 km at the beginning time of practicing the sport walking. The negative influence is marked by the number of the starts and the running training quantity. The cumulative effect of the training in the following years can influence on the progress of the results in the sport walking, especially in the 50 km distance. Practicing sport walking in 50 km should not cause any decrease of the efficiency in the sport walking's shorter distance.
