AB  - WEARABLE RESISTANCE (WR) PROVIDES THE PRACTITIONER WITH THE MEANS TO OVERLOAD SPRINT RUNNING IN A SPRINT-SPECIFIC MANNER. THIS ARTICLE INVESTIGATES THE EFFECTS OF WR ON SPRINT-RUNNING PERFORMANCE BY DISCUSSING THE MECHANISMS ASSOCIATED WITH WR, AS WELL AS THOSE FACTORS THAT MUST BE TAKEN INTO CONSIDERATION BY THE PRACTITIONER WHEN IMPLEMENTING A PROGRAM THAT USES WR. IN PARTICULAR, THE EFFECTS OF DIFFERENT WR BODY PLACEMENTS (TRUNK, LEGS, AND ARMS) WILL BE DISCUSSED. PRACTICAL APPLICATIONS AND CONCLUSIONS FROM THE ANALYSIS WILL BE PROVIDED.
